.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-RENAME-OBJECT 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-rename-object \- rename an object within its bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm rename-object
.BR \-\-bucket | \-b
.I ERN
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.BR \-\-new\-key | \-n
.I KEY
.SH DESCRIPTION
Renames an object within its bucket - the same operation as
.BR euclid-cli-esm-move-object (1)
with one bucket, said the way it is usually meant.
.PP
Nothing is copied, and the object keeps its content type, checksum and
attributes. Its ERN changes, because an ERN names a bucket and a key.
.PP
A key is a path only by convention: renaming
.I reports/2026/q3.csv
to
.I archive/q3.csv
moves it between what listings show as directories, because those
directories are only the prefixes of the keys a bucket holds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the bucket the object is in. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Current key of the object. Required.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Key it should have. Required.
.PP
The bucket may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The object was renamed. It is printed as JSON, under its new key.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, no session, the bucket does not exist or
belongs to another account, no object has that key, or something is
already stored under the new key.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli esm rename-object \e
    --bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000::bucket:inbox \e
    --key report.csv --new-key report-2026-09-01.csv
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-move-object (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-copy-object (1)
